<!--
    Premium/crown button in the Home header (btnPremium).

    Converted from the Figma header icon (118:441). Path data is verbatim
    from the export; the geometry is not redrawn.

    SIZING: the export is a 22.5x20 leaf; the group maps its 20-unit frame onto
    19.7 units of this 24 viewport — the ink height of ic_notification_bell,
    which is staying and is therefore the fixed reference every other header
    icon is matched to. That also lands within 1.5% of the design's own 20dp
    spec. scale 0.985 with translate (0.9188, 2.15) centres it.

    fillType is deliberately absent: the export carries no fill-rule, so it
    uses non-zero, which is Android's default too. Forcing evenOdd would
    invert the knockouts.

    The previous glyph was a plain angular zigzag (M3,8 L7,12 L12,5 ...) with
    no finials and no base band — a different icon, not a proportion problem
    (IoU 0.69). This is the designed crown: three ball-tipped points over a
    solid base.

    WIDEST GLYPH IN THE HEADER. Its frame is 22.5x20, so matched on height it
    spans x[0.92, 23.08] — under a unit of margin. Faithful to the design,
    where the crown genuinely outsizes its neighbours.
-->
